    "node-yu76gn": {
      "action": "keep",
      "reason": "The condition that the Utilities air gallery serves RHOB and local indication P-R normally shows normal pressure is supported by area directory records. The incident description confirms a loss of pressure in this specific system.",
      "replacementIds":[],"evidenceIds":["b678a928-a8d2-472d-bc03-2e1a3dc411e6"]},
    "node-13d0xmk": {
      "action": "keep",
      "reason": "The status of crew qualifications is unknown. The assignment extract (availableEvidence) has not been read to confirm if U-A/U-B held current certs at shift start.",
      "replacementIds":[],"evidenceIds":["7e69d300-c57e-40a8-bb37-35a61073ff33"]},
    "node-1qjpt5e": {
      "action": "keep",
      "reason": "The work package cover indicates the temporary instruction attachment field was blank. This is a procedural gap that may have contributed to missing specific safety instructions or hazard analysis for this maintenance task.",
      "replacementIds":[],"evidenceIds":["eaee59fe-70f4-4876-a21d-780814412078"]},
    "node-bcy6tj": {
      "action": "keep",
      "reason": "The maintenance acceptance signature was not yet signed at the time of notification. This indicates work preparation had not reached a formal 'ready' state, potentially leaving safety barriers (like isolation or verification) incomplete.",
      "replacementIds":[],"evidenceIds":["eaee59fe-70f4-4876-a21d-780814412078"]},
    "node-1k2yvh3": {
      "action": "keep",
      "reason": "RHOB reported an 'air-low' indication and requested Utilities attendance at ~10:00 AM. This is partially supported by the pressure drop record (p4) and alarm journal entry (AL-44), though exact timing alignment of the verbal report vs system trigger has uncertainty.",
      "replacementIds":[],"evidenceIds":["24ec1587-92e9-4320-82c2-30368d834f1d#1"]},
    "node-18lmyxb": {
      "action": "keep",
      "reason": "Utilities acknowledged receipt and paused work at ~10:02 AM. This is supported by the shift log timeline showing a pause in operations shortly after the 10:00 report.",
      "replacementIds":[],"evidenceIds":["kb:communication-supervision"]},
    "node-uusx8l": {
      "action": "keep",
      "reason": "Normal pressure returned at ~10:07 AM and records were requested. This is supported by the shift log showing restoration of supply.",
      "replacementIds":[],"evidenceIds":["24ec1587-92e9-4320-82c2-30368d834f1d"]}},"decision":{
    "summary":"The investigation board retains the core sequence: RHOB reports air-low -> Utilities acknowledges and pauses work. The causal chain is incomplete because we lack evidence of *why* the pressure dropped (source vs distribution) or if specific barriers were missing due to the unsigned acceptance/blank attachment.",
    "evidenceUsed":["24ec1587-92e9-4320-82c2-30368d834f1d","eaee59fe-70f4-4876-a21d-780814412078","b678a928-a8d2-472d-bc03-2e1a3dc411e6"],"unknowns":["Exact timing of 'air-low' report vs AL-44 alarm trigger.","Whether the blank attachment field contained critical safety instructions for this specific task.","If crew qualifications were current at shift start."],"alternatives":["The pressure drop was caused by a source failure (unlikely to resolve in 7 mins without intervention) or distribution valve closure due to upstream issue.","The 'air-low' indication might have been misinterpreted as normal fluctuation if the alarm threshold logic is unclear, though the record says it triggered an event."],"confidence":0.65},"evidenceRequests":[
    "requestId-req1","documentCoverage:IA-S02_work_package_cover.md#attachment_field_content",
    "rationale:The blank attachment field (node-1qjpt5e) is a procedural gap; we need to know if it was intentionally left blank or an error, and what specific instructions were missing for the compressor/dryer maintenance."
  ]}
